  "scope": "# Review: 27080597d778\n\nTask/source: `27080597d778` v2.0.0; production generator SHA-256 remains `dc379efc26f48130d6f42e7f52573ca74dfb4eccf407d467b741d94e832c37d9`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: current production was already approved, but this original ARC family lacked source-bound parametric evidence; added a task-local `fallback_panel={left,right}` prototype and auditor.\nReference-rule change: none. `left` is byte-exact canonical/default; `right` changes only the global-test failure fallback from copying the left panel to copying the right panel.\nEpisode contract: one fixed setting, four demonstrations, four distinct queries, all four branch profiles, and demonstrations reject the opposite declared setting before queries.\nConfound repair: paired seeds `2k`/`2k+1` now share `input_seed=k`, so visible inputs/order are fixed while only the rule changes.\nRacket evidence: two exact programs, all labels executed in protected Racket, independent Python parity, and 9/9 canonical pairs replayed under `left`.\nFocused verification: 17 prototype tests passed; full assigned generator suite 135 passed.\nAdversarial verification: 72 inputs / 144 Racket evaluations passed, balanced 18 per branch; export hash, source hash, privacy, numeric-type, duplicate-ID, and tamper checks passed.\nEvidence: `checks/parametric/fallback-panel-final/` and `checks/parametric/fallback-panel-adversarial.json`.\nStatus: main work complete; proposed `right` remains unapproved and is not admitted to production or training.",
